## 1. Core Concept: Pick / Not-Pick Framework

Every combination and permutation problem is built on a **decision tree** where at each step you make a choice about which element to include.

```
Two fundamental patterns:
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  COMBINATION pattern  (order doesn't matter)     │
│  → Pick / Not-Pick at each index                 │
│  → Move index forward to avoid duplicates        │
│                                                  │
│  PERMUTATION pattern  (order matters)            │
│  → Choose ANY remaining unused element           │
│  → Mark used, recurse, unmark (backtrack)        │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### The Backtracking Template (applies to ALL problems below)

```
solve(choices, current, result):
    if base_condition_met:
        result.add(copy of current)
        return

    for each valid choice:
        make choice       → add to current
        solve(...)        → recurse
        undo choice       → backtrack (remove from current)
```

> 🔑 **The backtrack step is mandatory.** Without it, choices from one branch bleed into another.

