## 4. Comparison: Combination Sum I vs II

```
┌─────────────────────┬──────────────────────┬──────────────────────┐
│ Aspect              │ Combination Sum I     │ Combination Sum II   │
├─────────────────────┼──────────────────────┼──────────────────────┤
│ Input               │ Distinct candidates  │ May have duplicates  │
│ Reuse               │ Unlimited reuse      │ Use each once only   │
│ Recurse with        │ index = i (same)     │ index = i+1 (next)   │
│ Duplicate skipping  │ Not required         │ Required (sort+skip) │
│ Sort needed?        │ For pruning only     │ Mandatory for dedup  │
│ Typical result size │ Smaller              │ Larger (more choices)│
└─────────────────────┴──────────────────────┴──────────────────────┘

Key line difference:
  Sum I:  backtrack(candidates, i,   ...)  // stay at i
  Sum II: backtrack(candidates, i+1, ...)  // move to i+1
```

