## 9. Interview Preparation Guide

### 🎯 Identifying the Problem Type in 30 Seconds

Ask yourself these questions in order:

```
Q1: Does order matter in the result?
    YES → Permutation   (start from index 0 each time)
    NO  → Combination   (start from current index)

Q2: Can I reuse the same element?
    YES → Stay at same index when picking
    NO  → Move to i+1 when picking

Q3: Are there duplicate values in input?
    YES → Sort + skip duplicate siblings at each level
    NO  → No special handling needed

Q4: Do I need all results, or just count/exists?
    ALL RESULTS → backtracking + collect
    COUNT ONLY  → memoization + DP (usually faster)
    EXISTS?     → early return on first valid path
```

### 🔴 Most Common Interview Mistakes

| Mistake | Symptom | Fix |
|---------|---------|-----|
| Forgetting to backtrack | Incorrect subsets, elements persist across branches | Always `remove(last)` after recursive call |
| Not copying the list | All results point to same (empty) list | Use `new ArrayList<>(current)` when adding |
| Wrong index on reuse | Infinite loop (reuse) or missing combos (no reuse) | Stay at `i` for reuse, `i+1` for no reuse |
| Missing duplicate skip | Duplicate results in output | Sort + `if (i > index && nums[i]==nums[i-1]) continue` |
| Wrong condition for permutation dup skip | Still getting duplicates | `!used[i-1]` not `used[i-1]` |
| Not sorting before duplicate handling | Random order makes deduplication incorrect | Always sort first when deduplication needed |

